@startuml
package a_$a #yellow {
  package java.lang #white {
    class foo$1
  }
}
a_$a --> dummy$2
@enduml

/' Regression introduced by the fix for issue #2846 (PR #2874, commit
350eb1e0bc69): CODE_BAREWORD in CommandPackage.java ("[%pLN_.]*") dropped
support for '$' in an unquoted, no-"as" package identifier, unlike the
permissive NAME group it replaced and unlike the '$'-inclusive identifier
regex used elsewhere for entities (see
CommandLinkClass.getClassIdentifier(), "[%pLN_$]+").

With the bug, "package a_$a { ... }" only captured "a_" as the package's
code, while the later reference "a_$a --> dummy$2" resolved via the
(unaffected) general entity-identifier regex to the full "a_$a" - a
different code from the package's. This split what should be a single
package into two entities: a package named "a_" plus a stray class
"a_$a", growing the diagram from 2 leaf entities to 3.
'/
